Epic: bd-01KXYJK0XSA3RNH9ANMVC96EPE

Implement and verify the generic APIs Gale must own before Scalafim can delete its local equivalents:
- pivoted QR with caller-controlled rank tolerance and explicit diagnostics;
- allocation-conscious matrix-RHS least-squares solve, Q and QT application, residualization support, and normalized covariance support;
- matrix-RHS Cholesky solve and explicit tolerance policy;
- shared efficient owned DMat construction or builder workspace without exposing raw backing storage;
- generic operator composition, adjoint or transpose values, batch matrix application, restrictions, and block operators where these are not domain semantics.

Acceptance
Public Gale contracts remain JVM and Scala.js portable, preserve storage encapsulation, have law and differential coverage, and include focused allocation and performance evidence for the Scalafim usage shapes. Domain-specific fMRI policy does not move into Gale. Any implementation work in the Gale checkout must use that repositories own tracker and path reservations.
